extraction_notes: "WB19 Australia printed 135-137 (cache p136-p138, cache page = printed folio + 1), read off the text layer in column order. The heading Kwarla Mystic R.C.C. and the eight numbered Powers of the Kwarla Mystic start on printed 135 and run through printed 136; the block headed Young Kwarla Mystics as an Optional Player Character R.C.C. starts at the foot of printed 136 and fills the first column of printed 137. || SPLIT: stored as an occupation limited to the kwarla race (the Dog Boy pattern, BOOK-INGEST-AUDIT F110), because the block gives Natural Abilities & Bonuses as the same as any Kwarla plus the Mystic''s powers. It is category occ so that it can pair with the race; occ_group magic is a reading (the class is both psychic and mage). men_of_arms is false: the race is a Mega-Damage creature. || XP: the Kwarla Mystic/Elder, Sham-Man/False Sorcerer ladder on the Experience Tables, printed 223, read off a render. || ATTRIBUTES: Attribute Modification +1D4+2 to I.Q., M.A., M.E. and P.E. is stored as attribute bonuses on top of the race''s dice. || P.P.E.: the block repeats the racial P.P.E. 4D6+22 and power 5 gives 1D6x10 + P.E. attribute number, +2D6 per level (the text layer prints !D6xlO). Power 5 is stored as ppe_base with overrides_race [ppe_base] so the Mystic''s figure replaces the race''s; that is a reading of two printed figures, and regression pins the carriers of overrides_race by name, so kwarla-mystic has to be added to that list in the PR. || PSIONICS (powers 2 and 3): master; I.S.P. is M.E. + 2D4x10 (printed 2D4xlO), +10 per level starting at level one, stored as M.E. + 2d4x10 + 10 with +10 per additional level. Mind Block, Exorcism and Meditation are granted. Three Sensitive or Healing powers OR one Super power is stored as the three; the Super alternative is in the group''s note and is not offered by the picker. Two more Sensitive or Healing are a second group. Two Sensitive and/or Healing powers at levels 2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12 and 14 and one Super power at levels 3, 6, 9 and 12 are the schedule. The race''s 1D4 Physical powers are restated here as a third starting group of four, because an occupation''s groups replace the race''s count in a pairing. || MAGIC (power 4): the six granted spells are catalog rows under the printed names (Globe of Daylight 1, Cleanse 2, Negate Mechanics 7, Power Weapon 8, Speed Weapon 10, Ironwood 12; the last three are far above the Mystic''s level and are granted by name as the book prints). Six spells of choice from levels one and two. Two new spells at each level from any level up to one beyond the character''s own is stored as fourteen schedule entries (level 2 picks from 1-3, and so on, capped at 15). Aboriginal Magic is described in a book not imported. || BONUSES (power 6): headed R.C.C. & Mystic Bonuses, so the figures are the Mystic''s totals and the race''s are not added again: +8 vs possession is stored as +1 over the race''s +7, +2 vs Ritual magic as +1 over the race''s +1, and +5 vs Horror Factor is the race''s own +5 and adds nothing. +4 vs mind controlling drugs, potions and magic charms is a saves.other line. The master psionic save of 10 comes with the tier. || SKILLS: Speaks Kwarla & Aboriginal at 80+3D6% is Language: Aboriginal at 80 with per_level 0; the 3D6 is not stored. Lore: Demon & Monsters is Lore: Demons & Monsters; Identify Plants & Fruits is Identify Plants & Fruit; Speaks English/Australian is Language: Australian English. The text layer runs the heading Natural Abilities: into O.C.C. Skills:; the Natural Abilities & Bonuses line is printed after the Secondary Skills. Hand to Hand: Basic only is costs {}. || RELATED: Medical Holistic and Pathology only is Holistic Medicine and Pathology. Physical except Hand to Hand skills is an except_prefix. Technical except Computers, Photography and others that use modern equipment is stored as Computer Operation, Computer Programming and Photography; the open-ended rest is in the note. W.P. any ancient is the book''s Ancient Weapon Proficiencies list (printed 152) plus W.P. Axe. || EQUIPMENT: the animal hide cloak or poncho is the poncho row and the wooden staff is the quarterstaff row; the beaded necklace has no catalog row and is in GM Notes. Millennium magic items are at the G.M.''s discretion. No money is printed, so no starting_money is stored. || NOT STORED: weight 200 + 5D6 pounds and life span 32 + 3D6 years (those past 40 live another 1D6x10 years as an Elder) differ from the race''s and are in GM Notes."
---

## Lore

Mystics lead Kwarla society. A Demon Hunter or a Provider may be chief, but
the Mystic is the power that manages the tribe and keeps its spirit. Every
tribe has one elder Mystic, perhaps an heir who is his friend and
assistant, and a few young ones preparing to leave. Even the young are
revered like medicine men; the elder is carried in a sedan chair, and
Kwarla and brave Aboriginals alike come to him for advice, cures and
stories.

Once every eight years the Mystic chooses a newborn by a small rite of
divination, watching the infant make its way to its mother''s pouch while
the tribe waits outside the hut. What he looks for is a secret passed only
to a successor. The child is raised as the Mystic''s own, something its
mother is proud of, and at adolescence is sent out alone into a dangerous
world to learn its truths and horrors at first hand. More than half do not
come back.

A Mystic is both psychic and mage. His magic is not learned; it arrives
through meditation and reflects the work of helping warriors, fighting the
supernatural and protecting the tribe.

## GM Notes

Pair this class with the Kwarla race, which carries the body: attributes,
M.D.C., claws, Claws of Vengeance and the racial bonuses. The Mystic adds
+1D4+2 to I.Q., M.A., M.E. and P.E.

Bonuses (power 6) are printed as the Mystic''s totals: +8 to save vs
possession, +2 vs Ritual magic, +5 vs Horror Factor and +4 vs mind
controlling drugs, potions and magic charms. The sheet adds only the
difference from the race''s own bonuses. As a master psionic the Mystic
saves vs psionic attack on a 10 or higher.

At level one the Mystic may take one Super Psionic power in place of three
Sensitive or Healing powers; the picker does not offer that trade. I.S.P.
grows by a flat 10 per level, which the level-up does not add by itself.

New spells at each level may come from any spell level up to one beyond
the Mystic''s own, from the wizard spells of the Rifts RPG and Federation of
Magic or from Aboriginal Magic.

As an NPC the Mystic''s divinations can be as cryptic as the G.M. likes. For
a player, answer each question vaguely: for a raid on a place of good magic
held by well-armed outlaws, something like a great risk bringing a great
reward.

50-65% of young Mystics die on their journey. Weight 200 + 5D6 pounds;
life span 32 + 3D6 years, and those who live past 40 are likely to live
another 1D6x10 years as a revered Elder (8th level or higher).

Starting kit beyond what the sheet lists: a beaded necklace. Any Millennium
magic items are at the G.M.''s discretion. The book prints no money.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'kwarla-mystic');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'kwarla-mystic';

-- Records this run. REQUIRED: the smoke test fails a data script that has no
-- footer, or whose footer names a different file.
INSERT INTO data_script_runs (filename) VALUES ('add-kwarla-mystic-class.sql');
